heretek-act1-presentation-title = ACT I
    UNKNOWN

heretek-act1-echo-001 = White noise gathers into a silhouette. It stands still, yet its outline lags behind itself.
heretek-act1-echo-002 = Where am I?
heretek-act1-echo-003 = Not here. “Here” is a word for places that remember their walls.
heretek-act1-echo-004 = This place has only your footsteps. As long as you walk, it does not vanish.
heretek-act1-echo-005 = What do you seek in the void?
heretek-act1-echo-choice-1 = A way out.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-1-selected = A way out.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-1-response = Every survivor looks for a door first. Then they learn the price of what they left beyond it.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-2 = You.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-2-selected = You.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-2-response = Then you are late. I was here before you, and yet I arrived after.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-3 = An answer.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-3-selected = An answer.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-3-response = In the Imperium, answers are issued with a seal. This one would fail every inspection.
heretek-act1-echo-006 = Do you remember a name, a face, the way you hold a weapon? Good. That does not mean you remember yourself.
heretek-act1-echo-007 = In the Koronus Expanse, people wear their past like armour: heavy, ill-fitting, and still unable to stop shrapnel.
heretek-act1-echo-008 = You speak as though you have seen Koronus.
heretek-act1-echo-009 = Who are you?
heretek-act1-echo-choice-4 = A warp-ghost.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-4-selected = A warp-ghost.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-4-response = The warp loves names. I lose mine as soon as I say them.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-5 = My enemy.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-5-selected = My enemy.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-5-response = If I were your enemy, I would show you the path that is easier to choose.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-6 = Someone who survived.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-6-selected = Someone who survived.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-6-response = Survival does not always mean remaining. Sometimes it means being the only one who remembers why.
heretek-act1-echo-010 = I saw ships without names and oaths without witnesses. I saw loyalty become a convenient word when provisions ran out.
heretek-act1-echo-011 = I saw one order save a deck, and another turn that same deck into a grave.
heretek-act1-echo-012 = The worst thing is not that darkness answers. It is when it speaks in your voice.
heretek-act1-echo-013 = What am I meant to do?
heretek-act1-echo-choice-7 = Obey the order.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-7-selected = Obey the order.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-7-response = An order may hold a line. It will not choose whom you leave behind a door.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-8 = Trust the Emperor.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-8-selected = Trust the Emperor.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-8-response = Faith gives light. It does not change the fact that your hand will hold the lever.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-9 = Decide for myself.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-9-selected = Decide for myself.
heretek-act1-echo-choice-9-response = Then do not hide the choice behind a beautiful name. Every decision has an owner.
heretek-act1-echo-014 = I did not come to foretell your death. Prophecy is a luxury for those who have already decided all is lost.
heretek-act1-echo-015 = I came because I saw you in futures where you became too useful to another will.
heretek-act1-echo-016 = Each began with a choice that seemed small at the time.
heretek-act1-echo-017 = Look. Eight paths. Eight ways to lose yourself or return to yourself.
heretek-act1-echo-018 = Who do you want to become?
heretek-act1-echo-choice-final = …
heretek-act1-echo-choice-final-selected = …
heretek-act1-echo-choice-final-response = Only you can decide who you become here.
heretek-act1-echo-019 = White noise splits into eight silhouettes.
heretek-act1-vision-001 = First: the warrant heir. The right to command became an excuse.
heretek-act1-vision-002 = Second: the nameless survivor. They kept their life after their name was sold.
heretek-act1-vision-003 = Third: the indebted trader. Their holds are full, but creditors own it all.
heretek-act1-vision-004 = Fourth: the tithe subject. They traded freedom for order and no longer argue.
heretek-act1-vision-005 = Fifth: the voidsman. They hear the reactor better than the people they left behind.
heretek-act1-vision-006 = Sixth: the guardsman. They saved a platoon with an order they could not forgive.
heretek-act1-vision-007 = Seventh: the forge adept. They replaced doubt with ritual and called it knowledge.
heretek-act1-vision-008 = Eighth: the Inquisition's tool. They cleansed a world and forgot whom they meant to protect.
heretek-act1-vision-009 = All of them were you. None is required to become you.
heretek-act1-fracture-001 = Look closer. The whiteness is not empty. It is cracking.
heretek-act1-fracture-002 = The first crack is always small. It needs only one name with nowhere left to return.
heretek-act1-fracture-003 = Time is running out. Do not cling to a place that has already decided to let you go.
heretek-act1-fracture-004 = When the fracture closes, take a step. Beyond it waits not an answer, but a beginning.
